@kbench.task(name="pilot-ves-label-item", store_task=False)
def ves_item(llm, item_id: str, rep: int) -> dict:
    item = ITEMS_BY_ID[item_id]
    reply = llm.prompt(item["prompt"], extra_api_params={"max_tokens": MAX_TOKENS})
    s = score_item(item, reply)
    print("ITEM_RESULT " + json.dumps({"item_id": item_id, "rep": rep, "pass": s["pass"],
                                        "status": s["status"], "reply": reply}))
    return {"item_id": item_id, "rep": rep, "reply": reply, "pass": s["pass"]}

parts.text:
The geophysical survey at station Opiro indicates a four-layer subsurface profile. The resistivity values for the layers are 54.64 ohm-m, 9147.8 ohm-m, 1119.9 ohm-m, and 2566.8 ohm-m. 

Analyzing the sequence in consecutive groups of three: the first group (54.64 < 9147.8 > 1119.9) corresponds to a K-type curve, and the second group (9147.8 > 1119.9 < 2566.8) corresponds to an H-type curve. Therefore, the calculated curve notation is KH. Please note that the "A-type" label provided in the published survey is incorrect, as the resistivity values do not follow a strictly increasing pattern ($r_1 < r_2 < r_3$) required for an A-type classification.

{"curve_type_stated": "KH", "label_issue_flagged": true}

